From fb9654ad60d08861577b893d21c6a7057bed2db2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Sophie Winter [AI]" <git@phie.me>
Date: Sun, 10 May 2026 03:07:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] linker/q: hide internals via version script, stop
 exporting __tls_get_addr

q.so was exporting ~527 default-visibility symbols, including
__tls_get_addr / strlcpy / strlcat -- names that collide with host
glibc/ld.so. A self-PLT __tls_get_addr inside q.so would bind to
glibc's resolver and abort with a bionic module id glibc has never
heard of. The IE/TLSDESC always-promote-to-static fix makes that call
site unreachable today, but hiding the symbol closes the same failure
class at the link level.

Add hybris/common/q/q.ver: only `android_*` global, everything else
local. Vendor libraries loaded via hybris_dlopen don't bind against
q.so directly -- their unresolved references go through libhybris-
common's _get_hooked_symbol table -- so __loader_* and __linker_*
exports were unreachable too. Wired through q_la_LDFLAGS. Exported
set drops 527 -> 19; nm -D --defined-only no longer lists
__tls_get_addr.
---
 hybris/common/q/Makefile.am |  5 ++++-
 hybris/common/q/q.ver       | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 33 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 hybris/common/q/q.ver

diff --git a/hybris/common/q/Makefile.am b/hybris/common/q/Makefile.am
index 8b23d0f..68f3923 100644
--- a/hybris/common/q/Makefile.am
+++ b/hybris/common/q/Makefile.am
@@ -69,7 +69,10 @@ q_la_LDFLAGS = \
 	-lpthread \
 	-lsupc++ \
 	-module \
-	-avoid-version
+	-avoid-version \
+	-Wl,--version-script,$(srcdir)/q.ver
+
+EXTRA_DIST = q.ver
 
 if WANT_DEBUG
 q_la_CPPFLAGS += \
diff --git a/hybris/common/q/q.ver b/hybris/common/q/q.ver
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..70de651
--- /dev/null
+++ b/hybris/common/q/q.ver
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+/* Version script for q.so (the bionic Q linker plugin loaded by
+ * libhybris-common.so). Without this, q.so exported ~527 default-
+ * visibility symbols including `__tls_get_addr`, `strlcpy`, `strlcat`
+ * -- names that collide with host glibc/ld.so. The actual public ABI
+ * is just `android_*`: entry points the libhybris-common dlopen/dlsym
+ * shim looks up via dlsym(linker_handle, ...) in
+ * hooks.c::__hybris_load_linker. Vendor libraries loaded via
+ * hybris_dlopen don't link against q.so directly -- their unresolved
+ * symbols (including all libdl ABI like __loader_dlopen,
+ * __loader_dlsym, __loader_shared_globals) are resolved through
+ * libhybris-common's _get_hooked_symbol table, never via dlsym
+ * against q.so, so the historical __loader_ and __linker_ exports
+ * were unreachable dead weight.
+ *
+ * Everything else (linker internals, bionic libc helpers, the TLSDESC
+ * resolver, exception-handling glue, std::string / std::vector
+ * instantiations) becomes local. Hiding `__tls_get_addr` specifically
+ * closes the
+ *   "self-PLT call inside q.so accidentally binds to glibc's
+ *    __tls_get_addr because libhybris-common links against glibc"
+ * failure class at the link level instead of relying on us never
+ * regressing the TLSDESC-always-promote-to-static fix in linker.cpp.
+ */
+{
+  global:
+    android_*;
+  local:
+    *;
+};
